# Union Alpha — EXCLUDED (no verified public benchmarks)

**Source / Date:** Independent web research, 2026-11-14 UTC.
**Exclusion reason:** Union Alpha is described not as a single pretrained model but as the stealth/test build of "Unbiased Pareto" — an inference-time multi-model *system* that runs several off-the-shelf models in parallel, then competes, filters, and dynamically synthesizes their outputs. Reviewed sources report no model-specific public benchmark figures (no SWE-bench, GPQA, LMArena, or context-window specification attributable to "Union Alpha" as a model). This matches the self-exclusion rule: with zero verified public benchmarks, no scored file is produced. Note this is the same "Pareto" lineage as `pareto-26.10-preview`, which was also excluded.

**What was checked:** Baidu Baike / Zhihu / benchmark explainers. The only substantive hit was a Zhihu discussion identifying Union Alpha as the stealth version of Unbiased Pareto and characterizing it as slow, not cheap, and built on an opaque underlying model pool.

**Recommended follow-up:** If/when a vendor publishes Union Alpha as a discrete model with spec sheet and benchmark numbers (rather than as a routing system), re-run research and produce a scored `Hy3.md`.

